---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";

const updated = "November 25, 2026";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy"
  description="What eldritchinc.com collects, why, how long it's kept, and how to have it removed. Nothing is sold."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="site-container privacy">
      <p class="eyebrow">Privacy</p>
      <h1 class="heading">Privacy policy</h1>
      <p class="updated">Last updated {updated}</p>

      <p class="lede">
        We collect very little, use it only for the reasons below, and never
        sell it.
      </p>

      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <p>
        <strong>Analytics, only if you accept.</strong> If you click Accept on
        the cookie banner, we load Google Analytics. It sets cookies and tells us which pages are visited, roughly where
        visitors are in the world, how they found the site, and whether they
        sign up or book a call. We don't use Google's advertising features or
        Google signals. If you decline, no analytics cookies are set and
        nothing is sent to Google.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>What you send us in a form.</strong> The release-notes signup
        collects your email address. The azathoth-team founding-team application
        collects your name, work email, company, team size, and anything you
        choose to tell us about how you'd use it.
      </p>
      <p>
        <strong>Basic server logs.</strong> Our host, Netlify, keeps standard
        request logs to run and protect the site.
      </p>

      <h2>Why</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Analytics: to see which pages help and improve the site.</li>
        <li>Release notes: to email you when Azathoth ships something new.</li>
        <li>Founding-team applications: to contact you about azathoth-team.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who handles it</h2>
      <p>
        Form submissions are received and stored by Netlify, which hosts this
        site. Analytics, if you accept, are processed by Google. We share your
        information with no one else, and we never sell it.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Analytics data: no more than 14 months.</li>
        <li>
          Form submissions: for as long as the list they're for exists, or
          until you ask us to remove them.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Your choices</h2>
      <p>
        You can change your analytics choice at any time:
        <button class="link-button" type="button" data-consent-reset>
          change cookie settings
        </button>.
        Every release-notes email will let you unsubscribe. To see, correct
        or delete anything we hold about you, email
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> and we'll take care
        of it.
      </p>

      <h2>Contact</h2>
      <p>
        {site.name}, {site.location}.
        <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>

<style>
  .privacy {
    max-width: 780px;
  }

  .updated {
    margin: 1rem 0 0;
    color: var(--color-muted);
    font-size: 0.9rem;
  }

  h2 {
    margin: 2.75rem 0 0.75rem;
    font-size: 1.4rem;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }

  p,
  li {
    color: #2c312c;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.75;
  }

  p {
    margin: 0 0 1rem;
  }

  ul {
    padding-left: 1.25rem;
  }

  a,
  .link-button {
    color: var(--color-accent);
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  .link-button {
    padding: 0;
    border: 0;
    background: none;
    cursor: pointer;
    text-decoration: underline;
  }
</style>
